    "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 01: Graded Reading\n\n## Course Overview\n\n### Course Type\n\nGraded Reading\n\n### Course Purpose\n\nThis course supports leveled picture-book reading through picture walk, teacher read-aloud, echo reading, pointing, choosing, movement, pretend play, and short oral responses. Each lesson centers on one Level AA book.\n\n### Relationship to PowerUp\n\nPowerUp provides the broad unit theme: **朋友与家人 / 家庭、亲情、晚安**. The graded reading books do not need to match PowerUp lesson-by-lesson; they provide leveled book language, picture-supported vocabulary, and light theme connections.\n\n### Unit Book Set\n\n| Week | Lesson Focus | Primary Book | Target Language |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| W1 | friends, family, and familiar people | AA Jungle Friends | This is _____. / I see _____. |\n| W2 | friends, family, and familiar people | AA My Easter | This is _____. / I see _____. |\n| W3 | friends, family, and familiar people | AA Eight | This is _____. / I see _____. |\n| W4 | friends, family, and familiar people | AA The Movie | This is _____. / I see _____. |\n\n# Lesson 1: Level AA - Jungle Friends\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Jungle Friends\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Jungle Friends*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`_____ friends.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nfriends, frog, jungle\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Jungle Friends* to explore friends, family, and familiar people through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Animal Action Parade: children choose animal cards from the book, move like each animal, then stop and say the animal word or the matching sound/action.\n2. Animal Sort and Home: children sort animals by sound, body part, covering, food, or home; after sorting, they place each animal on a simple habitat mat and name it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 2: Level AA - My Easter\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - My Easter\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *My Easter*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`my _____ holiday a partner.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nbasket, candy, dress, my, easter\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *My Easter* to explore friends, family, and familiar people through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Easter Basket Hunt: children hide and find basket, candy, dress, and holiday picture cards, then place each found item into a pretend Easter basket and name it.\n2. Holiday Table Build: children add Easter items to a celebration table or picture mat, match them to book pages, and say one key word for each item.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 3: Level AA - Eight\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Eight\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Eight*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`eight _____ dogs.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nfriends, backpacks, bottles, hot, sticks, raincoats, chairs, lights\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Eight* to explore friends, family, and familiar people through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Family and Feeling Photo Wall: children place family or feeling cards on a wall display; each child chooses one card, acts it out or gives it to a pretend family member, and repeats the useful book phrase.\n2. Kindness Delivery: children deliver a card, hug token, smile token, or bedtime item to a puppet/family picture, naming the item or feeling before placing it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 4: Level AA - The Movie\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - The Movie\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *The Movie*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`the _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nline, movie, popcorn, the\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *The Movie* to explore friends, family, and familiar people through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Family and Feeling Photo Wall: children place family or feeling cards on a wall display; each child chooses one card, acts it out or gives it to a pretend family member, and repeats the useful book phrase.\n2. Kindness Delivery: children deliver a card, hug token, smile token, or bedtime item to a puppet/family picture, naming the item or feeling before placing it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n",
