    "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 02: Graded Reading\n\n## Course Overview\n\n### Course Type\n\nGraded Reading\n\n### Course Purpose\n\nThis course supports leveled picture-book reading through picture walk, teacher read-aloud, echo reading, pointing, choosing, movement, pretend play, and short oral responses. Each lesson centers on one Level AA book.\n\n### Relationship to PowerUp\n\nPowerUp provides the broad unit theme: **在学校 / 校园场景**. The graded reading books do not need to match PowerUp lesson-by-lesson; they provide leveled book language, picture-supported vocabulary, and light theme connections.\n\n### Unit Book Set\n\n| Week | Lesson Focus | Primary Book | Target Language |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| W1 | school places and classroom objects | AA One | I see the _____. / This is school. |\n| W2 | school places and classroom objects | AA Yellow | I see the _____. / This is school. |\n| W3 | school places and classroom objects | AA BLUE | I see the _____. / This is school. |\n| W4 | school places and classroom objects | AA The City | I see the _____. / This is school. |\n\n# Lesson 1: Level AA - One\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - One\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *One*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`one _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\ndesk, bed, pillow, blanket, rug, window, book, toy\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *One* to explore school places and classroom objects through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. School-Day Mission: set up a small classroom or school map with desk, bed, pillow, blanket, and rug cards; children choose one card, use or echo `one _____.`, and move it to the place where it belongs.\n2. Ready for School Role-Play: children pack, carry, deliver, or arrange the book items in a pretend school routine, then finish by naming 2-3 items from the book together.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 2: Level AA - Yellow\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Yellow\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Yellow*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`the yellow _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nbus, cab, hat, light, lines, signs, truck, vest\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Yellow* to explore school places and classroom objects through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. School-Day Mission: set up a small classroom or school map with bus, cab, hat, light, and lines cards; children choose one card, use or echo `the yellow _____.`, and move it to the place where it belongs.\n2. Ready for School Role-Play: children pack, carry, deliver, or arrange the book items in a pretend school routine, then finish by naming 2-3 items from the book together.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 3: Level AA - BLUE\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - BLUE\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *BLUE*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`the blue _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nbench, bike, blue, bottle, helmet, playground, sky, slide\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *BLUE* to explore school places and classroom objects through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. School-Day Mission: set up a small classroom or school map with bench, bike, blue, bottle, and helmet cards; children choose one card, use or echo `the blue _____.`, and move it to the place where it belongs.\n2. Ready for School Role-Play: children pack, carry, deliver, or arrange the book items in a pretend school routine, then finish by naming 2-3 items from the book together.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 4: Level AA - The City\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - The City\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *The City*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`the _____ buildings.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nnoise, streets, cars, people, big, buses, park, stores\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *The City* to explore school places and classroom objects through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Floor Map Journey: place destination or vehicle cards around a floor map; children move a toy person/vehicle to one card and say or echo `the _____ buildings.`.\n2. Ticket and Station Game: children receive a ticket card, find the matching station, name the place or vehicle, and travel as a group to the next book location.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n",
