    "unitId": "k1-graded-reading-unit-03",
    "level": "K1",
    "courseType": "non-language",
    "track": "graded-reading",
    "courseCode": "B",
    "unitNumber": 3,
    "title": "Food and Drink",
    "displayTitle": "K1 Unit 03: Graded Reading",
    "status": "working-test-unit",
    "sourceRoot": "/Users/Lucia/Desktop/RAZ/graded_reading_lesson_designs",
    "sourceMarkdownPath": "/Users/Lucia/Desktop/RAZ/graded_reading_lesson_designs/K1_U03_Graded_Reading_Compact_Lesson_Plan.md",
    "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 03: Graded Reading\n\n## Course Overview\n\n### Course Type\n\nGraded Reading\n\n### Course Purpose\n\nThis course supports leveled picture-book reading through picture walk, teacher read-aloud, echo reading, pointing, choosing, movement, pretend play, and short oral responses. Each lesson centers on one Level AA book.\n\n### Relationship to PowerUp\n\nPowerUp provides the broad unit theme: **食物与饮品 / 食物、饮品、购物**. The graded reading books do not need to match PowerUp lesson-by-lesson; they provide leveled book language, picture-supported vocabulary, and light theme connections.\n\n### Unit Book Set\n\n| Week | Lesson Focus | Primary Book | Target Language |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| W1 | food, color, plants, and garden vocabulary | AA Red | I see _____. / It is _____. |\n| W2 | food, color, plants, and garden vocabulary | AA Orange | I see _____. / It is _____. |\n| W3 | food, color, plants, and garden vocabulary | AA The Plant | I see _____. / It is _____. |\n| W4 | food, color, plants, and garden vocabulary | AA My Garden | I see _____. / It is _____. |\n\n# Lesson 1: Level AA - Red\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Red\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Red*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`the red _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\napple, beet, cherry, pepper, potato, radish, red, strawberry\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Red* to explore food, color, plants, and garden vocabulary through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Make a Pretend Plate: children choose food cards such as apple, beet, cherry, pepper, and potato, put them on a tray or plate, and say the food word or echo the book phrase before serving it.\n2. Food Shop Helper: set up a tiny food shop; children buy, sell, or pack one item from the book and name it before putting it in a bag or lunchbox.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 2: Level AA - Orange\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Orange\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Orange*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`an orange _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nbutterfly, field, flower, leaf, orange, pumpkin, snake, sunset\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Orange* to explore food, color, plants, and garden vocabulary through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Animal Action Parade: children choose animal cards from the book, move like each animal, then stop and say the animal word or the matching sound/action.\n2. Animal Sort and Home: children sort animals by sound, body part, covering, food, or home; after sorting, they place each animal on a simple habitat mat and name it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 3: Level AA - The Plant\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - The Plant\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *The Plant*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`the _____ plant.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\ndirt, shovel, baby, sunshine, hole, seed, rain\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *The Plant* to explore food, color, plants, and garden vocabulary through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Nature Investigator: children inspect picture cards or realia for dirt, shovel, baby, sunshine, and hole; they place each item under see, touch, grow, fall, or live and explain with one word or short phrase.\n2. Sequence the Nature Story: children arrange 3-5 book pictures into a simple order, then walk a finger through the sequence while naming key words from the book.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 4: Level AA - My Garden\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - My Garden\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *My Garden*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`my _____ ideas with a partner.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\ngarden, hoe, hose, my\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *My Garden* to explore food, color, plants, and garden vocabulary through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Nature Investigator: children inspect picture cards or realia for garden, hoe, hose, and my; they place each item under see, touch, grow, fall, or live and explain with one word or short phrase.\n2. Sequence the Nature Story: children arrange 3-5 book pictures into a simple order, then walk a finger through the sequence while naming key words from the book.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n",
