    "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 04: Graded Reading\n\n## Course Overview\n\n### Course Type\n\nGraded Reading\n\n### Course Purpose\n\nThis course supports leveled picture-book reading through picture walk, teacher read-aloud, echo reading, pointing, choosing, movement, pretend play, and short oral responses. Each lesson centers on one Level AA book.\n\n### Relationship to PowerUp\n\nPowerUp provides the broad unit theme: **居家生活 / 居家空间**. The graded reading books do not need to match PowerUp lesson-by-lesson; they provide leveled book language, picture-supported vocabulary, and light theme connections.\n\n### Unit Book Set\n\n| Week | Lesson Focus | Primary Book | Target Language |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| W1 | home spaces and home objects | AA This Kitchen | My _____. / I see _____. |\n| W2 | home spaces and home objects | AA My Closet | My _____. / I see _____. |\n| W3 | home spaces and home objects | AA My Bath | My _____. / I see _____. |\n| W4 | home spaces and home objects | AA The Backyard | My _____. / I see _____. |\n\n# Lesson 1: Level AA - This Kitchen\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - This Kitchen\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *This Kitchen*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`This ____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nstove, sink, fridge, cupboard, counter, toaster, cookie jar, trash can\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *This Kitchen* to explore home spaces and home objects through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Make a Pretend Plate: children choose food cards such as stove, sink, fridge, cupboard, and counter, put them on a tray or plate, and say the food word or echo the book phrase before serving it.\n2. Food Shop Helper: set up a tiny food shop; children buy, sell, or pack one item from the book and name it before putting it in a bag or lunchbox.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 2: Level AA - My Closet\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - My Closet\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *My Closet*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`My ____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nhangers, shirts, pants, dresses, shoes, belts, blankets, closet\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *My Closet* to explore home spaces and home objects through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Dress the Character: children choose clothing cards such as hangers, shirts, pants, dresses, and shoes, dress a puppet or paper character, and name each item before adding it.\n2. Closet Sort: children sort clothing cards by where they go, who wears them, or what weather they match, then pack the chosen outfit into a pretend bag.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 3: Level AA - My Bath\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - My Bath\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *My Bath*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`My ____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\ntub, water (recurs from U3 L4), bubbles, toys (recurs as a theme from U6, but the word appears here first in K1), soap, shampoo, towel, bath\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *My Bath* to explore home spaces and home objects through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Floor Map Journey: place destination or vehicle cards around a floor map; children move a toy person/vehicle to one card and say or echo `My ____.`.\n2. Ticket and Station Game: children receive a ticket card, find the matching station, name the place or vehicle, and travel as a group to the next book location.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 4: Level AA - The Backyard\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - The Backyard\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *The Backyard*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`The ____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nfence, dog, swing, ball, flowers, tree, hose, backyard\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *The Backyard* to explore home spaces and home objects through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Animal Action Parade: children choose animal cards from the book, move like each animal, then stop and say the animal word or the matching sound/action.\n2. Animal Sort and Home: children sort animals by sound, body part, covering, food, or home; after sorting, they place each animal on a simple habitat mat and name it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n",
