    "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 05: Graded Reading\n\n## Course Overview\n\n### Course Type\n\nGraded Reading\n\n### Course Purpose\n\nThis course supports leveled picture-book reading through picture walk, teacher read-aloud, echo reading, pointing, choosing, movement, pretend play, and short oral responses. Each lesson centers on one Level AA book.\n\n### Relationship to PowerUp\n\nPowerUp provides the broad unit theme: **假期玩耍户外冬天 / 寒假、户外、玩耍、夏令营**. The graded reading books do not need to match PowerUp lesson-by-lesson; they provide leveled book language, picture-supported vocabulary, and light theme connections.\n\n### Unit Book Set\n\n| Week | Lesson Focus | Primary Book | Target Language |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| W1 | holiday, seasons, and outdoor play | AA Winter | It is _____. / We go _____. |\n| W2 | holiday, seasons, and outdoor play | AA We Go Camping | It is _____. / We go _____. |\n| W3 | holiday, seasons, and outdoor play | AA The Coast | It is _____. / We go _____. |\n| W4 | holiday, seasons, and outdoor play | AA Summer | It is _____. / We go _____. |\n\n# Lesson 1: Level AA - Winter\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Winter\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Winter*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`The ____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nsnow, ice skates, sled, snowman, mittens, coat, fire, winter\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Winter* to explore holiday, seasons, and outdoor play through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Nature Investigator: children inspect picture cards or realia for snow, ice skates, sled, snowman, and mittens; they place each item under see, touch, grow, fall, or live and explain with one word or short phrase.\n2. Sequence the Nature Story: children arrange 3-5 book pictures into a simple order, then walk a finger through the sequence while naming key words from the book.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 2: Level AA - We Go Camping\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - We Go Camping\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *We Go Camping*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`Our ____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\ndrive, spot, tools, tent, fire (recurs from L1 — same word, different context), food, stories, camp\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *We Go Camping* to explore holiday, seasons, and outdoor play through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Make a Pretend Plate: children choose food cards such as drive, spot, tools, tent, and different context), put them on a tray or plate, and say the food word or echo the book phrase before serving it.\n2. Food Shop Helper: set up a tiny food shop; children buy, sell, or pack one item from the book and name it before putting it in a bag or lunchbox.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 3: Level AA - The Coast\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - The Coast\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *The Coast*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`The ____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nocean (recurs from U3 L4 Water), waves, beach, rocks, cliff, birds (recurs from U8), lighthouse, coast\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *The Coast* to explore holiday, seasons, and outdoor play through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Animal Action Parade: children choose animal cards from the book, move like each animal, then stop and say the animal word or the matching sound/action.\n2. Animal Sort and Home: children sort animals by sound, body part, covering, food, or home; after sorting, they place each animal on a simple habitat mat and name it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 4: Level AA - Summer\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Summer\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Summer*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`the _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nsummer, sunshine, rain, garden, flowers, beach, swimsuit, ball\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Summer* to explore holiday, seasons, and outdoor play through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Nature Investigator: children inspect picture cards or realia for summer, sunshine, rain, garden, and flowers; they place each item under see, touch, grow, fall, or live and explain with one word or short phrase.\n2. Sequence the Nature Story: children arrange 3-5 book pictures into a simple order, then walk a finger through the sequence while naming key words from the book.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n",
