    "courseCode": "B",
    "unitNumber": 6,
    "title": "Toys",
    "displayTitle": "K1 Unit 06: Graded Reading",
    "status": "working-test-unit",
    "sourceRoot": "/Users/Lucia/Desktop/RAZ/graded_reading_lesson_designs",
    "sourceMarkdownPath": "/Users/Lucia/Desktop/RAZ/graded_reading_lesson_designs/K1_U06_Graded_Reading_Compact_Lesson_Plan.md",
    "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 06: Graded Reading\n\n## Course Overview\n\n### Course Type\n\nGraded Reading\n\n### Course Purpose\n\nThis course supports leveled picture-book reading through picture walk, teacher read-aloud, echo reading, pointing, choosing, movement, pretend play, and short oral responses. Each lesson centers on one Level AA book.\n\n### Relationship to PowerUp\n\nPowerUp provides the broad unit theme: **玩具 / 玩具、搭建**. The graded reading books do not need to match PowerUp lesson-by-lesson; they provide leveled book language, picture-supported vocabulary, and light theme connections.\n\n### Unit Book Set\n\n| Week | Lesson Focus | Primary Book | Target Language |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| W1 | toys, building, and position words | AA Play Ball | I play with _____. / It is _____. |\n| W2 | toys, building, and position words | AA Toys | I play with _____. / It is _____. |\n| W3 | toys, building, and position words | AA We Build | I play with _____. / It is _____. |\n| W4 | toys, building, and position words | AA Over | I play with _____. / It is _____. |\n\n# Lesson 1: Level AA - Play Ball\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Play Ball\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Play Ball*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`A ____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nball (recurring anchor noun across all 8 items), beach ball, baseball, basketball, football, tennis ball, golf ball, soccer ball\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Play Ball* to explore toys, building, and position words through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Floor Map Journey: place destination or vehicle cards around a floor map; children move a toy person/vehicle to one card and say or echo `A ____.`.\n2. Ticket and Station Game: children receive a ticket card, find the matching station, name the place or vehicle, and travel as a group to the next book location.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 2: Level AA - Toys\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Toys\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Toys*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`The ____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nblocks, bear, paint (noun here — \"the paint\" as a creative-supply toy; recurs as a verb in L3), drum, plane, wagon, kite, robot\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Toys* to explore toys, building, and position words through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Animal Action Parade: children choose animal cards from the book, move like each animal, then stop and say the animal word or the matching sound/action.\n2. Animal Sort and Home: children sort animals by sound, body part, covering, food, or home; after sorting, they place each animal on a simple habitat mat and name it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 3: Level AA - We Build\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - We Build\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *We Build*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`We ____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\ndraw, saw, sand, hammer, drill, paint (verb here — \"we paint\" the project; same word appears as a noun in L2), glue, hang\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *We Build* to explore toys, building, and position words through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Build and Present: children use blocks, paper pieces, or object cards to build/make one item from the book, then present it with the book word or frame.\n2. Helper Workshop: children take pretend helper roles, choose tools/materials, and complete a tiny job such as build, fix, sort, or recycle before naming what they used.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 4: Level AA - Over\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Over\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Over*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`over the _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\ncat, log, pot, doll, ball, hole, bike, bat\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Over* to explore toys, building, and position words through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Animal Action Parade: children choose animal cards from the book, move like each animal, then stop and say the animal word or the matching sound/action.\n2. Animal Sort and Home: children sort animals by sound, body part, covering, food, or home; after sorting, they place each animal on a simple habitat mat and name it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n",
