    "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 08: Graded Reading\n\n## Course Overview\n\n### Course Type\n\nGraded Reading\n\n### Course Purpose\n\nThis course supports leveled picture-book reading through picture walk, teacher read-aloud, echo reading, pointing, choosing, movement, pretend play, and short oral responses. Each lesson centers on one Level AA book.\n\n### Relationship to PowerUp\n\nPowerUp provides the broad unit theme: **玩与自然 / 自然、动物、季节**. The graded reading books do not need to match PowerUp lesson-by-lesson; they provide leveled book language, picture-supported vocabulary, and light theme connections.\n\n### Unit Book Set\n\n| Week | Lesson Focus | Primary Book | Target Language |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| W1 | nature, animals, and seasons | AA Jump Over | I see _____. / It is _____. |\n| W2 | nature, animals, and seasons | AA These Birds | I see _____. / It is _____. |\n| W3 | nature, animals, and seasons | AA It Is Fall | I see _____. / It is _____. |\n| W4 | nature, animals, and seasons | AA The Ocean | I see _____. / It is _____. |\n\n# Lesson 1: Level AA - Jump Over\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Jump Over\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Jump Over*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`the _____ jumps over.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\ncow, cat, dog, girl, goat, horse, fox, deer\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Jump Over* to explore nature, animals, and seasons through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Animal Action Parade: children choose animal cards from the book, move like each animal, then stop and say the animal word or the matching sound/action.\n2. Animal Sort and Home: children sort animals by sound, body part, covering, food, or home; after sorting, they place each animal on a simple habitat mat and name it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 2: Level AA - These Birds\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - These Birds\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *These Birds*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`these _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nbirds, crows, doves, eagles, geese, hawks, owls, turkeys\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *These Birds* to explore nature, animals, and seasons through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Animal Action Parade: children choose animal cards from the book, move like each animal, then stop and say the animal word or the matching sound/action.\n2. Animal Sort and Home: children sort animals by sound, body part, covering, food, or home; after sorting, they place each animal on a simple habitat mat and name it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 3: Level AA - It Is Fall\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - It Is Fall\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *It Is Fall*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`the _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\njacket, leaf, moon, apple, rake, acorn, corn, pumpkin\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *It Is Fall* to explore nature, animals, and seasons through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Fall Collection Walk: children collect or choose fall cards such as jacket, leaf, moon, apple, and rake, then place each item on a fall table and name it.\n2. Build a Fall Scene: children add fall picture cards to a seasonal scene, act out one fall action such as rake or wear a jacket, and match it to the book page.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 4: Level AA - The Ocean\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - The Ocean\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *The Ocean*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`The ____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nwater (recurs from U3 L4 Water and U4 L3 My Bath), sand, coral, seaweed, fish, crab, starfish, ocean (recurs from U3 L4 Water and U5 L3 The Coast)\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *The Ocean* to explore nature, animals, and seasons through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Animal Action Parade: children choose animal cards from the book, move like each animal, then stop and say the animal word or the matching sound/action.\n2. Animal Sort and Home: children sort animals by sound, body part, covering, food, or home; after sorting, they place each animal on a simple habitat mat and name it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n",
