    "unitNumber": 9,
    "title": "All About Me",
    "displayTitle": "K1 Unit 09: Graded Reading",
    "status": "working-test-unit",
    "sourceRoot": "/Users/Lucia/Desktop/RAZ/graded_reading_lesson_designs",
    "sourceMarkdownPath": "/Users/Lucia/Desktop/RAZ/graded_reading_lesson_designs/K1_U09_Graded_Reading_Compact_Lesson_Plan.md",
    "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 09: Graded Reading\n\n## Course Overview\n\n### Course Type\n\nGraded Reading\n\n### Course Purpose\n\nThis course supports leveled picture-book reading through picture walk, teacher read-aloud, echo reading, pointing, choosing, movement, pretend play, and short oral responses. Each lesson centers on one Level AA book.\n\n### Relationship to PowerUp\n\nPowerUp provides the broad unit theme: **关于我自己 / 大小、衣物、介词、认知**. The graded reading books do not need to match PowerUp lesson-by-lesson; they provide leveled book language, picture-supported vocabulary, and light theme connections.\n\n### Unit Book Set\n\n| Week | Lesson Focus | Primary Book | Target Language |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| W1 | self, size, clothing, and position words | AA Big | It is _____. / The _____ is _____. |\n| W2 | self, size, clothing, and position words | AA Little | It is _____. / The _____ is _____. |\n| W3 | self, size, clothing, and position words | AA Six | It is _____. / The _____ is _____. |\n| W4 | self, size, clothing, and position words | AA Under | It is _____. / The _____ is _____. |\n\n# Lesson 1: Level AA - Big\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Big\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Big*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`a big _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\ndinosaur, house, dog, elephant, tree, car, bus, plane\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Big* to explore self, size, clothing, and position words through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. School-Day Mission: set up a small classroom or school map with dinosaur, house, dog, elephant, and tree cards; children choose one card, use or echo `a big _____.`, and move it to the place where it belongs.\n2. Ready for School Role-Play: children pack, carry, deliver, or arrange the book items in a pretend school routine, then finish by naming 2-3 items from the book together.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 2: Level AA - Little\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Little\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Little*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`a little _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nbaby, house, dog, mouse, car, bug, plane, tree\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Little* to explore self, size, clothing, and position words through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Animal Action Parade: children choose animal cards from the book, move like each animal, then stop and say the animal word or the matching sound/action.\n2. Animal Sort and Home: children sort animals by sound, body part, covering, food, or home; after sorting, they place each animal on a simple habitat mat and name it.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 3: Level AA - Six\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Six\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Six*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`six _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\nhats, shirts, pants, gloves, coats, dresses, shorts, socks\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Six* to explore self, size, clothing, and position words through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. Dress the Character: children choose clothing cards such as hats, shirts, pants, gloves, and coats, dress a puppet or paper character, and name each item before adding it.\n2. Closet Sort: children sort clothing cards by where they go, who wears them, or what weather they match, then pack the chosen outfit into a pretend bag.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n\n\n# Lesson 4: Level AA - Under\n\n## Core Book: Level AA - Under\n\n### Source\n\n- **Book:** Level AA - *Under*\n- **PDF:** TBD\n- **Audio:** TBD\n- **Video:** TBD\n- **Lesson Plan:** TBD\n- **Worksheet:** TBD\n\n### Language Pattern\n\n#### Sentence Frame\n\n`under the _____.`\n\n#### Key Vocabulary\n\ntree, chair, desk, swing, umbrella, table, bed, pillow\n\n### Story Context\n\nChildren use *Under* to explore self, size, clothing, and position words through pictures, repeated language, and a short classroom task.\n\n### Suggested Activities / Games\n\n1. School-Day Mission: set up a small classroom or school map with tree, chair, desk, swing, and umbrella cards; children choose one card, use or echo `under the _____.`, and move it to the place where it belongs.\n2. Ready for School Role-Play: children pack, carry, deliver, or arrange the book items in a pretend school routine, then finish by naming 2-3 items from the book together.\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n- Look at the picture.\n- Point to the _____.\n- Say it with me.\n- Read with me.\n- What do you see?\n- Good reading.\n",
